+
+/* xemu aa54c34cae, nxdk_pgraph_tests' Fog carryover: a program's oFog starts as the value the
+ * last program left in it, so one writing no oFog under FOG_ENABLE is fogged by that (Blade 2).
+ * xemu runs each program draw's last vertex on the CPU; here only what a later draw may need is
+ * kept: after a draw whose program writes oFog, that program, the current attribute values and
+ * the constants it reads (all of them where it indexes by A0); the CPU runs it when a draw
+ * that reads the carried value comes (a program writing no oFog, fog on). Until the first such
+ * draw nothing is copied but the attributes: its constants are then the current ones if
+ * nothing changed them since, else the carried value stays the reset's. As xemu's, the
+ * vertex is the attributes' current values, not the draw's last array vertex. */
